  "content": {
    "title": "No. 1 UConn women roll over UTSA in March Madness: NCAA highlights, score",
    "text": "Updated March 21, 2026, 5:51 p.m. ETFollow all the games today on USA TODAY Sports.STORRS, CT ― The No. 1 seed UConn women's basketball team made short work of its first-round assignment, No. 16 seed UTSA, in the NCAA Tournament Saturday, March 21.Four UConn players were in double figures in the 90-52 victory over UTSA. Sarah Strong had 18 points, Blanca Quiñonez 15, Ashlynn Shade 14 and Kayleigh Heckel 11.The Huskies were 7-for-33 from 3-point land. UConn coach Geno Auriemma was exasperated postgame that his players weren't concentrating on scoring in the paint, where they were dominating. UConn outscored UTSA in the paint 48-18.\"(We think if) we keep shooting them, they'll start going in,\" Auriemma said. \"That's how you lose games. So you have to come into these games, and you gotta go where you can get the points.\"At one point, we were 8 for 11 in the lane. And we're, at that time, one for 17 from three. You can't be all one way.\"The Huskies are now 35-0 and face the winner of Iowa State-Syracuse in the second round on Monday. The defending national champions have a 51-game win streak dating back to last season.USA TODAY Studio IX: Check out our women's sports hub for in-depth analysis, commentary and more End of Q3: UConn 75, UTSA 30Sarah Strong has 18 points, five rebounds, four assists and five steals as the No. 1 team in the country is cruising to its 50th straight win. Ashlynn Shade has 14 points and six rebounds and Blanca Quiñonez 12 points, five rebounds and three steals. UConn has 34 points off turnovers and 38 points in the paint. Halftime: UConn 48, UTSA 14Sarah Strong has 12 points, Ashlynn Shade 11 and Blanca Quiñonez 10 as the Huskies have jumped out to big lead at the half. UConn has 24 points off 19 turnovers by UTSA. The Huskies are outscoring the Roadrunners 28-4 in the paint. Breanna Stewart in the crowd End of 1Q: UConn 19, UTSA 6Sarah Strong scored nine points as the Huskies built a double-digit halftime lead. They had some trouble getting their offense going off the long layoff since the Big East Tournament, shooting 39% from the field. UConn has 10 points in the paint and nine off turnovers. Huskies score firstSareh Williams gets the scoring started for UConn with the first four points of the game as we are underway in Storrs, Connecticut.What time is UTSA vs UConn first-round game?No. 1 UConn vs No. 16 UTSA tips off at 3:00 PM (ET) on Saturday, March 21 from Harry A. Gampel Pavilion (Storrs, Connecticut).What channel is UTSA vs UConn first-round game?No. 1 UConn vs No. 16 UTSA is airing live on ABC.How to stream UTSA vs UConn first-round gameNo. 1 UConn vs No. 16 UTSA is available to stream on Fubo.Stream Women's March Madness on Fubo UTSA starting five UConn starting five ESPN in the house UTSA on the way Huskies locked inWomen's March Madness schedule todaySee the schedule, live scores and results for all of Saturday's NCAA Tournament action here.2026 Women's NCAA Tournament full scheduleMarch 18-19: First FourMarch 20-21: First RoundMarch 22-23: Second RoundMarch 27-28: Sweet 16March 29-30: Elite 8April 3: Final FourApril 5: National ChampionshipJoin the USA TODAY Survivor Pool to win cash prizes",
